concept namespaces {
  name     = "Namespaces"
  summary  = "Scope declarations under a dotted path; use and :: control how names resolve."
  related  = [use_declarations, qualified_kinds, imports, identifiers, schema]
  audience = :both
  body {
    p "A `namespace` declaration scopes a file's declarations under a dotted path, `use` pulls names from other namespaces into local scope, and a `ns::kind` qualifier picks a block schema from a specific namespace. Together they let independently-authored libraries share a document without name collisions."
    h2 "Declaring a namespace"
    p "`namespace` takes a dotted path and must be the **first item** in the file. Every declaration then lives under that path: with `namespace company`, a `type Point` is fully qualified `company.Point`. A dotted declaration name nests further — `type utils.Point` becomes `company.utils.Point`."
    code "wcl" { source = <<'SRC'
namespace company

type utils.Point  { x: f64  y: f64 }
type shapes.Circle { center: utils.Point  radius: f64 }
SRC
    }
    p "Imported files keep their own `namespace` — an `import` brings their declarations in, but the names stay qualified under the imported file's path. See [Imports & Modules](concept_imports)."
  }
}
